      <div>
        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · Islamic Caliphates &amp; Middle East</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Isfahan</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">6th century BCE or earlier – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">No founding date is known: the area was inhabited from the Palaeolithic, the site became a regional centre under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a>, and a diverse city is recorded under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a>, whose edict of 538 BCE is the first date connected with it.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the plain of the Zayandeh River at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros Mountains</a>, 440 kilometres south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a>, in Isfahan Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Seljuk capital under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-shah-i">Malik-Shah I</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>'s massacre of 1387; Abbas the Great's capital from 1598; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naqsh-e-jahan-square">Naqsh-e Jahan Square</a> and the Chahar Bagh boulevard; the bridges over the Zayandeh; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-julfa">New Julfa</a> and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a>; the proverb 'Isfahan is half the world'</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Isfahan is the capital of Isfahan Province and the third most populous city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, with a population of about 2,238,000.</span></div>
